#: freeports_dev.page_view.INK_RAMP:1 of
msgid ""
"Grey levels map onto these, lightest first. Ten steps is as much as a "
"terminal font distinguishes."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.page_view.ROW_TOLERANCE:1 of
msgid ""
"How far apart two lines may start, vertically, and still be one row of "
"one table. Corpora in these documents arrive with a long decimal tail, "
"and 231.9 and 232.0 are one row."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.page_view.ascii_preview:3 of
msgid ""
"The row count is derived from the aspect ratio and then halved, because a"
" character cell is about twice as tall as it is wide and an un-halved "
"preview comes out stretched."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.page_view.document_image_counts:3 of
msgid ""
"A whole-document walk, so it is asked for rather than assumed: on a "
"report of eleven hundred pages it is seconds, and the per-page count "
"answers most questions."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.page_view.font_legend:3 of
msgid ""
"First appearance rather than alphabetical order, so that re-reading a "
"page after an edit does not renumber every tag because one line changed "
"font."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.page_view.ink_ratio:3 of
msgid ""
"A cheap answer to \"is this box ticked\", which is the question most "
"often asked of a small image in these documents."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.page_view.nearest_lines:3 of
msgid ""
"What an image *means* is whatever is written beside it: the tick mark of "
"an SFDR form is identified by the ``Yes`` or ``No`` it sits next to, "
"never by its own appearance."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.page_view.nearest_lines:6 of
msgid ""
"More than one, because the nearest line is often not the informative one."
" A tick in a form sits a few points below its section heading and a dozen"
" points left of its own label, so the single closest line is the heading "
"— true, and not what was being asked. Three lines cost three rows and "
"take the guessing out of it."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.page_view.nearest_lines:11 of
msgid ""
"The direction is decided by which gap is the larger, so a label on the "
"same row as the image reads as ``left`` or ``right`` even when it is also"
" very slightly higher."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.page_view.overlapping_indices:3 of
msgid ""
"Boxes that merely touch along an edge do not count: adjacent cells of a "
"table share a boundary by construction, and marking every one of them "
"would mark the whole page."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.page_view.page_images:3 of
msgid ""
"Through the engine's own extractor rather than by walking the dictionary "
"here, so that an image this tool shows is an image a pipe can see — "
"including the degenerate boxes the engine drops."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.page_view.reading_order:3 of
msgid ""
"`order` is ``\"y\"`` -- top to bottom, then left to right -- or "
"``\"x\"``, which reads each column of the page down before moving right. "
"`columns` splits the page into that many vertical bands and finishes each"
" band before starting the next, which is what a page carrying two tables "
"side by side needs: ordering such a page by ordinate alone interleaves "
"the two tables' rows."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.page_view.reading_order:8 of
msgid ""
"An order this function does not know is an error, not a fallback to the "
"default. A sort order silently replaced by another is a page read in an "
"order nobody chose."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.page_view.render_images:3 of
msgid ""
"Each image gets its box, its size on the page and in pixels, its digest "
"with how often that same digest occurs, the nearest text with the "
"direction it lies in, and a preview of the rendered region with its ink "
"ratio."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.page_view.render_images:7 of
msgid ""
"The digest is there because it answers the first question one has about a"
" small repeated image: the five marks of an SFDR form on one page turn "
"out to be one image used five times, and a single column of output says "
"so. The nearest text is there because it is what the image *means*: a "
"tick is identified by the ``Yes`` or ``No`` beside it, never by its own "
"appearance."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.page_view.render_lines:3 of
msgid ""
"Returns the rows rather than printing them, so the caller decides where "
"they go and the arrangement can be tested without capturing output."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.page_view.rendered_gray:3 of
msgid ""
"**Not** the bytes the page dictionary carries for the image. Those are "
"frequently not the picture: in these reports a tick mark is stored as a "
"solid black rectangle whose shape lives in a separate mask the dictionary"
" does not carry, so previewing the stored bytes shows a black square for "
"every tick on the page. Rendering the region applies the mask, the "
"transparency and anything drawn over or under it, which is the only "
"definition of \"what is there\" that matches the person checking the PDF "
"by eye."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.page_view.resample:3 of
msgid ""
"Averaging rather than sampling: a tick mark one pixel wide disappears "
"entirely from a preview that picks one source pixel per output cell, and "
"disappearing is the one failure a preview must not have."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.page_view.show_codepoints:3 of
msgid ""
"This is what tells a box glyph from a letter. A checkbox in these reports"
" is sometimes ``U+2612``, sometimes ``U+26AB`` in a symbol font, and on a"
" terminal both are a smudge or a replacement square."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.page_view.stored_size:3 of
msgid ""
"Worth a column of its own beside the box: a 13-pixel image drawn into a "
"9-point box is a glyph scaled up, and one drawn into a 200-point box is a"
" scan. That ratio is the first thing that tells you which kind of thing "
"you are looking at."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.page_view.stored_size:7 of
msgid ""
"A failure to decode is reported and not raised. Some stored streams are "
"not standalone images at all, and the point of this view is to look at a "
"page one does not yet understand."
msgstr ""

